<ProseLayout
  title="Standards"
  description="The published filter behind every Selected by Men ranking: what we look at, what we do not claim, how often a list is revisited, and what happens when a pick disappears."
  eyebrow="The filter"
  heading="Standards"
>
  <p>
    This page is the named source of judgment on Selected by Men. A ranking is
    the desk’s ranking against this filter. It is not a lab report, and it is
    not a paid placement.
  </p>

  <h2>The filter</h2>
  <p>Every recommendation has to clear the same questions:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Is the design considered, or just loud?</li>
    <li>Will it still feel right in a year?</li>
    <li>Is the price honest for the materials and construction?</li>
    <li>Do verified owners report the same strengths we care about?</li>
    <li>Is it worth telling a friend to buy it?</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    If the answer is no, it does not go on the list. How well a link converts
    does not override that.
  </p>

  <h2>What we actually look at</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Manufacturer specifications and the current US Amazon listing: real name,
      ASIN, what is in the kit, price band, water rating, battery, replacement
      parts.
    </li>
    <li>
      Star rating and review volume on that listing. A 4.8 with forty reviews is
      not the same evidence as a 4.3 with eight thousand.
    </li>
    <li>
      Independent editorial reviews when they exist, labeled as theirs — not
      ours.
    </li>
    <li>
      Cost to own: heads, cartridges, proprietary chargers, whether parts will
      still be sold.
    </li>
    <li>Who it is for, and who should skip it.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not invent lab tests. If a guide is not a thirty-day wear test, the
    guide says so. Manufacturer claims — closeness to the micron, cutting
    actions per minute, “below skin level” — stay labeled as claims.
  </p>

  <h2>How often a list is revisited</h2>
  <p>Live roundups are checked at least every 90 days, and sooner if:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>the product is discontinued or the listing dies</li>
    <li>a successor ships</li>
    <li>a material claim in the guide is wrong</li>
    <li>the price band moves enough that the recommendation changes</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The published date and the updated date on a guide are the dates that work
    happened. We do not backdate a piece to look older than the site.
  </p>

  <h2>If a pick disappears</h2>
  <p>
    We replace it, or we change the ranking and say why. We do not leave a dead
    buy link sitting as if it were still the pick. A temporary Amazon stock-out
    is a stock problem, not an automatic demotion — unless it stays gone.
  </p>

  <h2>Corrections</h2>
  <p>
    Write <a href="mailto:contact@selectedbymen.com">contact@selectedbymen.com</a>.
    A factual error gets a fix and a new updated date. A ranking change gets a
    sentence in the guide.
  </p>

  <h2>Money</h2>
  <p>
    This page is the editorial filter. How the site is paid is <a href="/how-we-make-money/">How we make money</a>. They are separate on
    purpose.
  </p>

  <p><em>Last updated August 28, 2026.</em></p>
</ProseLayout>
